.TH SELEVER 1 "2026-07-30" "Selever" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
selever \- install an exact toolchain or package and print its shell environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B node
.I version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B npm
.I package@version
.BI \-\-node= version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B go
.I version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B gopkg
.I package@version
.BI \-\-go= version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B batch
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B selever
installs the selected toolchain or package in an immutable directory and writes
the shell code needed to add its executables to
.BR PATH .
Progress and diagnostics are written to standard error.
.PP
All versions passed to
.B selever
must be exact.
Package installations are identified by both the package version and the parent
toolchain version.
Completed installations are reused without network access.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "node " version
Install an exact Node.js release.
The version must not have a leading
.BR v .
.TP
.BI "npm " package@version " \-\-node=" version
Install an exact npm package using the specified exact Node.js release.
.TP
.BI "go " version
Install an exact Go release.
The version must not have a leading
.BR go .
.TP
.BI "gopkg " package@version " \-\-go=" version
Build and install an exact Go package using the specified exact Go release.
A leading
.B v
on the module version is optional.
.TP
.B batch
Read selectors from standard input and emit one environment update.
See
.BR "BATCH INPUT" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-shell= shell
Select the format written to standard output.
Accepted values are
.BR auto ,
.BR sh ,
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
.BR pwsh ,
.BR powershell ,
.BR nu ,
and
.BR nushell .
The default is
.BR auto ,
which detects the invoking shell and falls back to
.BR sh .
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.SH BATCH INPUT
.B selever batch
reads one selector per non-empty line.
Fields are separated by whitespace.
Processing stops at the first invalid selector or failed installation.
The final environment update contains the executable directories from every
successful selection, in input order.
.PP
.EX
selever batch <<'EOF'
go 1.18
gopkg --go=1.18 golang.org/x/tools/gopls@0.14.2
EOF
.EE
.SH OUTPUT
For sh, bash, and zsh,
.B selever
writes an
.B export PATH=
command.
For fish it writes a
.B set \-gx PATH
command, and for PowerShell it writes an assignment to
.BR $env:PATH .
For Nushell it writes a JSON object suitable for
.BR load-env .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate default data and cache directories.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Overrides the data directory base.
The default is
.BR $HOME/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Overrides the cache directory base.
The default is
.BR $HOME/.cache .
.TP
.B SHELL
Used as a fallback when automatic shell detection cannot identify the parent
process.
.TP
.B HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY
Control proxies for HTTP metadata and download requests.
.TP
.B GOPROXY
Controls module lookup while installing Go packages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-$HOME/.local/share}/selever
Immutable toolchain and package installations.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:\-$HOME/.cache}/selever
Downloaded metadata and archives.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B selever
exits with status 0 after the selection is installed and the environment update
is written.
It exits non-zero if its arguments or batch input are invalid, shell detection
is overridden with an unsupported value, or an installation fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install Node.js 22.14.0 and print its environment update:
.PP
.EX
selever node 22.14.0
.EE
.PP
Install TypeScript 5.8.2 using Node.js 22.14.0:
.PP
.EX
selever npm typescript@5.8.2 --node 22.14.0
.EE
.PP
Resolve a non-exact version before installing it:
.PP
.EX
selever node "$(fetchver node 22)"
.EE
.SH NOTES
Node.js and Go archives are checksum-verified.
npm retains its native integrity and lifecycle behavior.
Installations are completed in a staging directory and moved into place
atomically while holding an exclusive lock for the installation identity.
.PP
Supported platforms are macOS and glibc Linux on amd64 and arm64.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fetchver (1),
.BR globver (1)
